    "title": "Children hunt for Kentucky Lake fossils, create cave art - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kenna Williams, Jason Thomason ,\n23 hours ago PADUCAH — Local children had the opportunity to become geologists Tuesday, sifting through Kentucky rocks and fossils at the McCracken County Public Library. John Tillson, retired geologist, led his Fossil Hunting and Cave Painting program, where children created cave paintings with their hands, learned about local fossils and searched for treasures of their own. Read full article\n1",
